{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Behold, its blood was not brought inside the sanctuary.</b> The atonement that applies to all the commandments, which is for the priest and for the congregation. And if one asks: behold the sin-offering bull is burned, yet its blood was not brought inside the sanctuary — the reason is the parokhet and the golden altar. Know that the sin-offering bull is for a sin upon the altar, and the goat of the sin-offering is for the people, and the flesh of the sin-offering is for the priest." "<b>You shall surely eat.</b> It was fitting that you eat it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Resolved הפרכת as haplography/variant spelling of הפרוכת (the veil/parokhet); the sense requires it and the following ומזבח הזהב confirms a list of sanctuary furnishings."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:21.459596374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}